'''tippet''' (tip′et), ''n.'' [Formerly also ''tippit''; < ME. ''tippet'', ''tipet'', ''tipit'', ''typet'', ''tepet'', < AS. ''tæppet'', a tippet (cf. ''tæpped'', tapestry, carpet, ''tæppe'', a fillet, band), < L. ''tapete'', ML. also ''tapetum'', < Gr. τάπης, figured cloth, tapestry, carpet, rug, coverlet, etc.: see ''tappet''<sup>1</sup>.] '''1.''' (''a'') A long and narrow pendent part of the dress, as the hanging part of a sleeve or the liripipium. (''b'') Any scarf or similar garment.

{{smaller block|Biforn hire wolde he go
With his ''typet'' ybounde about his heed.
{{right|''Chaucer'', Reeve's Tale, l. 33.}}}}

